        "id": 136847,
        "name": "JimB",
        "username": "JimB",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jimb/{size}/2093_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-03-08T06:46:07.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I refuse to play the Ennead in Silver Gulch 18whatever.  Nuit when flipped shuffles the environment trash into the environment deck, so if “Lost in the Past” is in play and you don’t have environment destruction in your hand, guess what, game over next round.</p>\n<p>It’s something that can be strategized around if you know to look out for it, but it’s one of those things that just makes me mad because it’s a totally unfair way to lose the game.</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:13:06.900Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
